# The environment the test suite boots with - deliberately empty.
#
# tests/Pest.php points WBACK_ENV here before any application is created.
# bootstrap/app.php takes the first environment file it finds, and WBACK_ENV is
# looked at before the project's own .env, so a developer's .env - and
# /etc/wback/.env - take no part in a test run. That is what lets a test putenv()
# a value and then refreshApplication(): the project .env is loaded mutably and
# would otherwise overwrite it.
#
# Why not .env.testing, the stock Laravel name: it does not work here. Laravel only
# reaches for .env.testing from its own loader, which is immutable - and by then
# bootstrap/app.php has already loaded the project .env mutably, so the developer's
# values are in place and .env.testing cannot override any of them. Tried, with
# APP_ENV=testing forced: the timezone tests still failed. WBACK_ENV is wback's own
# mechanism and runs first, which is the whole point.
#
# Keep this file free of values. A test that needs one sets it itself.
